{% extends 'base.html.twig' %}
{% block title %}Connect your own AI agent{% endblock %}
{% block page_content %}
<div class="row justify-content-center">
<div class="col-lg-9">
    <h1>Connect your own AI agent</h1>
    {% embed '@SurvosAiChat/mcp_connect.html.twig' with {
        name: 'Symfony Packages',
        endpoint: publicUrl ~ '/mcp',
        server: 'packages',
        checkout: 'packages',
        back: {url: path('ask'), label: 'Ask the catalog'},
        lead: 'Find Symfony bundles and PHP libraries for a need, with their Symfony and PHP support, downloads, releases and READMEs, from your own AI assistant. The connector is read-only and needs no account.',
        claude_code_prompt: 'Use packages to find a memory-friendly XML parser for TEI documents in a Symfony 7.4 app.',
        tool_descriptions: {
            find_packages: 'Find packages for a need in plain words (“stream large XML files”). Optionally only bundles, only a Symfony version, or also outdated (rejected) packages.',
            get_package: 'Read one package by name: constraints, require list, links and the start of its README.',
            search_packagist: 'Search packagist.org itself, for libraries the catalog does not hold; says whether each is catalogued.',
            catalog_stats: 'Exact counts of packages by status, bundles and rejection reasons.',
        },
        prompt: 'Use Symfony Packages to recommend what to use in a Symfony 7.4 app that manages TEI-encoded XML, with memory-friendly parsing. Say whether a dedicated bundle exists, give downloads and last release for each option, and warn about abandoned ones.',
        footnotes: ['The catalog covers Symfony bundles and the libraries around them, not every PHP library; search_packagist covers the rest.'],
    } %}
        {% block local_note %}
            <p class="mb-0">The app reads its local database, Elasticsearch and AI configuration; you do not paste any provider keys into your agent. <code>find_packages</code> embeds the question with the app’s embedding model (Ollama) and falls back to keywords when it is down.</p>
        {% endblock %}
        {% block tools_note %}
            <p>These tools read the catalog; they do not change it. Unlike the <a href="{{ path('ask') }}">chat on this site</a>, an outside agent decides which tools to call.</p>
        {% endblock %}
        {% block check %}
            <p>For a quick connection check, ask your agent to call <code>get_package</code> with <code>name: prewk/xml-string-streamer</code>. It should return “Stream large XML files with low memory consumption”.</p>
        {% endblock %}
    {% endembed %}
</div>
</div>
{% endblock %}
